config BR2_PACKAGE_REGLINUX_GAMES_DATABASES
	bool "REG-Linux games databases"
	help
	  Downloads the Redump.org, GameTDB and MAME offline databases,
	  gzipped, into /usr/share/reglinux/datainit/bios/databases
	  (unpacked to /userdata/bios/databases on first boot).

	  Redump.org/GameTDB (databases/) let regmsgd's scraper resolve an
	  optical disc's printed serial number straight to its known
	  checksum, without having to hash the whole disc image. MAME's own
	  "-listxml" release (mame/, stripped down to just name/year/
	  manufacturer/rotation/players) lets regmsgd's arcade library
	  resolve exact screen-rotation and metadata for the whole MAME/
	  FBNeo/Naomi/Atomiswave family, even on targets with no real mame
	  binary of their own.

	  https://redump.org
	  https://www.gametdb.com
	  https://www.mamedev.org
